SOAPBOX: Tried it low power usually could work much of what I heard (who could hear me, according to PSK Reporter). The exception was FT4 which didn't seem to work well for me at 100w with my topography so only 19 of my QSOs were FT4.
SOAPBOX: Generally a slow contest. Highest hourly rate was only 26. 90% CQ'ing to avoid worrying about dupes (wasn't using logger).
SOAPBOX: Probably could have done better if I paid more attention... the "80% waiting and then split second decision," model of FT8 operation is not compatible with the human brain, in my opinion.
SOAPBOX: Still, worked all continents, including 33 DXCCs and at least one new one on digital (Moldova).
